1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,420
Did you know your eyes are

2
00:00:01,320 --> 00:00:03,560
covered by a constantly renewing layer

3
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:04,120
of tears,

4
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:05,720
even when you're not crying?

5
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,240
This protective layer is called the

6
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:08,940
tear film,

7
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:11,020
and it actually consists of three

8
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:12,080
important components.

9
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,300
The outer,

10
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:14,200
oily layer,

11
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:16,100
produced by tiny glands in your

12
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:16,560
eyelids,

13
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:18,440
slows down evaporation.

14
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:19,640
Beneath it,

15
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:22,100
a watery layer delivers oxygen and

16
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:22,500
nutrients,

17
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,100
washes away dust,

18
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,440
and contains proteins that help fight

19
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:28,000
harmful microorganisms.

20
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:29,320
The innermost,

21
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:31,920
mucous -rich layer helps tears spread

22
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:33,740
evenly across the surface of your

23
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:34,080
eye.

24
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:35,880
But here's something fascinating.

25
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:37,680
Every time you blink,

26
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:40,740
your eyelids redistribute this delicate film,

27
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:42,260
keeping your eyes smooth,

28
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:42,980
protected,

29
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,200
and ready to focus light properly.

30
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:48,300
So why is yawning contagious?

31
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:50,020
Want to know the answer?

32
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:51,600
Watch our next video,

33
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:53,140
and don't forget to follow us

34
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:55,160
for more amazing facts about your

35
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:55,460
body.
